      "content": "But carrying it... it's not just heavy. it's hollow. It feels like there is nothing left of the man I was, just this shell of shame. I look at my blade and I don't see a tool for protection anymore, I just see the one thing that could finally bring some peace. A way to balance the scales. To atone. Isn't that what people do? When they've lost everything, when they've lost their honor... don't they find a way to end the shame properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
